-- title:
--   Idelic Artin map for a modulus whose unit idèles are norms
-- statement:
--   Let $F/E$ be a Galois extension of number fields whose Galois group $\mathrm{Gal}(F/E)$ is commutative, and let $\mathfrak f$ be a nonzero ideal of $\mathcal O_E$ with the following two properties. First, $\mathfrak f$ is divisible by every finite place $v$ of $E$ at which the inertia subgroup of $\mathrm{Gal}(F/E)$ attached to the chosen prime `primeAbove E F v` of $\mathcal O_F$ above $v$ is nontrivial. Second, the subgroup `unitIdeles E 𝔣` of the idèle group $(\mathbb A_E)^\times$ — consisting of those $u$ whose finite component has valuation $1$ at every finite place, satisfies $|u_v-1|\le \exp(-\operatorname{ord}_v\mathfrak f)$ at every $v\mid\mathfrak f$, and is positive under every real embedding $\tau\colon E\to\mathbb R$ — is contained in the image of the idelic norm $(\mathbb A_F)^\times\to(\mathbb A_E)^\times$ attached to the base change `genuineBaseChange E F`, that is, the unit map of the algebra norm of $\mathbb A_F$ over $\mathbb A_E$. Then there exists a group homomorphism $r\colon(\mathbb A_E)^\times\to\mathrm{Gal}(F/E)$ such that the principal idèles $E^\times$ lie in $\ker r$, $\ker r$ equals the subgroup generated by $E^\times$ together with the image of the idelic norm, $r$ is surjective, and for every idèle $u$ satisfying `IsAdjuster E 𝔣 u 1` (valuation $1$ and congruence to $1$ modulo $\mathfrak p_v^{\operatorname{ord}_v\mathfrak f}$ at each $v\mid\mathfrak f$, positivity at each real embedding) one has $r(u)=\prod^{\mathrm f}_{v} \mathrm{Frob}_v^{\,\operatorname{ord}_v(u_v)}$, the finite product over all finite places of the arithmetic Frobenius `artinFrob E F v` raised to $\operatorname{ord}_v$ of the finite component of $u$ at $v$.
--
--   This is Artin reciprocity in idelic form for an abelian extension of number fields, stated for a modulus $\mathfrak f$ that merely contains the ramified places and is deep enough that its congruence unit idèles are global norms, rather than for an admissible modulus. It is used in the computation of idèle class norm groups for cyclic extensions and in showing that $[F:E]$-th powers of norm idèles lie in the product of the principal idèles with the norm group.
